{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,17]],"date-time":"2026-09-17T19:08:48Z","timestamp":1789672128762,"version":"4.0.1"},"reference-count":34,"publisher":"American Geophysical Union (AGU)","issue":"9","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,9,18]],"date-time":"2015-09-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1442534400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":17,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,9,1]],"date-time":"2015-09-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1441065600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000181","name":"Air Force Office of Scientific Research","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["FA9550\u201012\u20101\u20100401"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["FA9550\u201012\u20101\u20100401"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000181","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["JGR Space Physics"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2015,9]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    The temporal and spatial variations of the thermospheric mass density during a series of idealized substorms were investigated using the Global Ionosphere Thermosphere Model (GITM). The maximum mass density perturbation of an idealized substorm with a peak variation of hemispheric power (HP) of 50\u2009GW and interplanetary magnetic field (IMF)\n                    <jats:italic>\n                      B\n                      <jats:sub>z<\/jats:sub>\n                    <\/jats:italic>\n                    of \u22122\u2009nT was ~14% about 50\u2009min after the substorm onset in the nightside sector of the auroral zone. The mass density response to different types of energy input has a strong local time dependence, with the mass density perturbation due to only an IMF\n                    <jats:italic>\n                      B\n                      <jats:sub>z<\/jats:sub>\n                    <\/jats:italic>\n                    variation peaking in the dusk sector and the density perturbation due to only HP variation peaks in the nightside sector. Simulations with IMF\n                    <jats:italic>\n                      B\n                      <jats:sub>z<\/jats:sub>\n                    <\/jats:italic>\n                    changes only and HP changes only showed that the system behaves slightly nonlinearly when both IMF and HP variations are included (a maximum of 6% of the nonlinearity) and that the nonlinearity grows with energy input. The neutral gas heating rate due to Joule heating was of same magnitude as the heating rate due to precipitation, but the majority of the temperature enhancement due to the heating due to precipitation occurs at lower altitude as compared to the auroral heating. About 110\u2009min after onset, a negative mass density perturbation (~\u22125%) occurred in the night sector, which was consistent with the mass density measurement of the CHAMP satellite.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/2014ja020962","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2015,8,22]],"date-time":"2015-08-22T18:53:01Z","timestamp":1440269581000},"page":"7987-8001","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":4,"title":["A simulation study of the thermosphere mass density response to substorms using GITM"],"prefix":"10.1029","volume":"120","author":[{"given":"Xianjing","family":"Liu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Atmospheric, Oceanic and Space Sciences University of Michigan  Ann Arbor Michigan USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Aaron","family":"Ridley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Atmospheric, Oceanic and Space Sciences University of Michigan  Ann Arbor Michigan USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"13","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2015,9,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2011JA017259"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/JA088iA08p06275"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","volume-title":"Aeronomy, Part B","author":"Banks P. M.","year":"1973"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.asr.2008.10.031"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/2014JA019837"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2003JA010176"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2010GL043671"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/JA092iA07p07606"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0021-9169(81)90142-2"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2000GL003771"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s11207-005-6393-4"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2011JA016994"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/2013JA019453"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jastp.2006.08.011"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/95JA00766"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_17_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2004GL021269"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_18_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Marcos F. A. S. T.Lai C. Y.Huang C. S.Lin J. M.Retterer S. H.Delay andE. K.Sutton(2010) Towards next level satellite drag modeling paper AIAA 2010\u20107840 presented at the AIAA Atmospheric and Space Environments Conference Toronto Ont. Canada 2\u20135 Aug.","DOI":"10.2514\/6.2010-7840"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_19_1","volume-title":"Auroral Plasma Physics","author":"Paschmann G.","year":"2002"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_20_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/JA086iA04p02385"},{"key":"e_1_